.TH ERC 1 "March 2026" "Version @VERSION@"

.SH NAME
erc \- a universal archive tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B erc
.RI [options]
.RI [command]
.RI name
.RI [target]
.PP
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BI
ERC is a universal command-line archive manager that provides a unified interface
for working with various archive formats. It uses patool as the primary backend,
with 7z as a fallback when patool is not available.
.PP
When extracting, erc decides where to place files:
.IP \(bu 2
Single file in archive \(em extracted to the current directory.
.IP \(bu 2
Single directory in archive \(em renamed to match the archive basename.
.IP \(bu 2
Multiple files or directories \(em extracted into a subdirectory named after the archive.
.PP
Use
.B erc basename
to see the predicted directory name for an archive.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B a, create, pack, add
Create archive or add files to archive.
.TP
.B x, extract, unpack
Extract files from archive.
.TP
.B l, list
List archive contents.
.TP
.B t, test, check
Test archive integrity.
.TP
.B type
Print archive type.
.TP
.B basename
Print the predicted directory name for the archive.
.TP
.B repack, conv
Convert archive to another format.
.TP
.B formats
List supported archive formats.
.TP
.B b, bench, benchmark
Run CPU benchmark.
.TP
.B diff
Compare two archives (requires patool).
.TP
.B search, grep
Search in archive files (requires patool).
.PP
Commands can also be used with a dash prefix: \fB\-a\fR, \fB\-x\fR, \fB\-l\fR, \fB\-t\fR, \fB\-b\fR.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Quiet mode.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Force override target.
.TP
.B \-C DIR
Extract to specified directory. The directory is created if it does not exist.
.TP
.B \-\-directory DIR, \-\-extract\-to DIR, \-\-destination DIR, \-\-outdir DIR
Same as \fB\-C\fR. Long options also accept \fB=\fR syntax (e.g. \fB\-\-directory=DIR\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-here, \-\-no\-subdir
Extract to current directory (or \fB\-C\fR directory) without creating a subdirectory.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-flat, \-\-junk\-paths
Extract all files without directory structure (strip paths).
.TP
.B \-\-use\-patool
Force use patool as backend.
.TP
.B \-\-use\-7z
Force use 7z as backend.

.SH EXAMPLES
 # erc a archive.zip file(s)... \- pack files to archive.zip
 # erc file(s)... zip: \- pack file(s) to zip archive
 # erc dir \- pack directory to dir.zip
 # erc [x] archive.zip \- unpack archive
 # erc \-C dir archive.zip \- extract directly into dir
 # erc \-\-here archive.zip \- extract without creating subdirectory
 # erc \-\-flat archive.zip \- extract all files stripping paths
 # erc l archive.zip \- list files of the archive
 # erc [repack] archive1.zip 7z: \- repack to 7z
 # erc [repack] archive.zip archive.7z \- repack zip to 7z
 # erc \-f repack archive.zip archive.7z \- repack (override target)
 # erc basename archive.tar.gz \- print predicted directory name
 # erc type archive.zip \- print archive type

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ERC_BACKEND
Set to \fBpatool\fR or \fB7z\fR to force a specific backend.

.SH BUGS
Please report any bugs to lav@etersoft.ru
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B erc
will return zero on success and non zero on operation failure.
